  "note": "All 84 passages are covered exactly once. Equations, tables and figures with empty or near-empty text were placed with the text they derive or illustrate (e.g. P31/P40/P47/P48 tables of moduli with their modulus subtopic; P43 with Example 8.4; P57/P59 with the beam-bending text; P68/P70 with the stress-strain exercise figures). Summary (P64) and Points to Ponder (P65) are chapter-wide but open on stress and strain, so they sit with that subtopic. Exercise passages (P66-P84) were assigned to the subtopic each question tests. The short cluster on why a mountain's maximum height is ~10 km (P62-P63) reads apart from the engineering examples in 8.6 and was given its own subtopic. Two passages carry stale cross-references from an earlier edition's numbering: P37 says 'from Eq. (9.4)' and P39 says 'Table 9.2'; these were left exactly as written."
